  "verbalization": "Cespitularin C appears to interact with Dr hemagglutinin structural subunit through multiple indirect pathways, all of which involve the enzyme ADP-ribosylation factor-like protein 3 or Sn1-specific diacylglycerol lipase beta. These proteins are targets of specific compounds, which in turn are linked to the hemagglutinin structural subunit. The evidence suggests that Cespitularin C may modulate the activity of these enzymes, potentially influencing the structural integrity or function of Dr hemagglutinin. The shared involvement of these proteins in the signaling pathways of the target compound and the hemagglutinin structural subunit implies a possible mechanism of action that involves enzyme inhibition or regulation. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Cespitularin C in the regulation of hemagglutinin, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
